  <li class="arxiv-result">
    <div class="is-marginless">
      <p class="list-title is-inline-block"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.21251">arXiv:2602.21251</a>
        <span>&nbsp;[<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.21251">pdf</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/ps/2602.21251">ps</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/format/2602.21251">other</a>]&nbsp;</span>
      </p>
      <div class="tags is-inline-block">
        <span class="tag is-small is-link tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Software Engineering">cs.SE</span>
        
          
            <span class="tag is-small is-grey tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Artificial Intelligence">cs.AI</span>
          
            <span class="tag is-small is-grey tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Multiagent Systems">cs.MA</span>
          
            <span class="tag is-small is-grey tooltip is-tooltip-top" data-tooltip="Programming Languages">cs.PL</span>
          
        </div>
      
    </div>
    
    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        AgenticTyper: Automated Typing of Legacy Software Projects Using Agentic AI
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Pohle%2C+C">Clemens Pohle</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2602.21251v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;systems lack type safety, making maintenance risky. While TypeScript can help, manually adding types is expensive. Previous automated typing research focuses on type <span class="search-hit mathjax">inference</span> but rarely addresses type checking setup, definition generation, bug identification, or behavioral correctness at repository scale. We present AgenticTyper, a Large Language Model (&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2602.21251v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2602.21251v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2602.21251v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Legacy JavaScript systems lack type safety, making maintenance risky. While TypeScript can help, manually adding types is expensive. Previous automated typing research focuses on type <span class="search-hit mathjax">inference</span> but rarely addresses type checking setup, definition generation, bug identification, or behavioral correctness at repository scale. We present AgenticTyper, a Large Language Model (<span class="search-hit mathjax">LLM</span>)-based agentic system that addresses these gaps through iterative error correction and behavior preservation via transpilation comparison. Evaluation on two proprietary repositories (81K LOC) shows that AgenticTyper resolves all 633 initial type errors in 20 minutes, reducing manual effort from one working day.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2602.21251v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2602.21251v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 21 February, 2026; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> February 2026.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Comments:</span>
      <span class="has-text-grey-dark mathjax">Accepted at ICSE 2026 Student Research Competition (SRC)</span>
    </p>
    

    
      <p class="comments is-size-7">
        

        

        
          <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">ACM Class:</span>
          D.2.3; D.2.7; F.3.3; I.2.2; I.2.11
        
      </p>
    

    
  </li>

  <li class="arxiv-result">
    <div class="is-marginless">
      <p class="list-title is-inline-block"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.20195">arXiv:2602.20195</a>
        <span>&nbsp;[<a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.20195">pdf</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/ps/2602.20195">ps</a>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/format/2602.20195">other</a>]&nbsp;</span>
